{"_v":1,"id":"amelie-a-new-musical-2017","cat":"broadway","cs":46.27,"rc":7,"bd":{"positive":0,"mixed":3,"negative":4},"rv":[{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":61,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2017/04/03/theater/amelie-musical-broadway-review-phillipa-soo.html","d":"2017-04-04","q":"“Amélie” the musical seems to have no nationality, or sensibility, to call its own."},{"cn":"Adam Feldman","o":"Time Out New York","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/newyork/theater/amelie-a-new-musical","d":"2017-04-03","q":"The show has a sweetness that is hard to resist, even when its whimsy occasionally crosses the line into preciousness."},{"cn":"Peter Marks","o":"The Washington Post","s":38,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/entertainment/theater_dance/review-amelie-a-new-musical-needs-more-than-whimsy-to-succeed/2017/04/04/8b0c6e7e-196a-11e7-9887-1a5314b56a08_story.html","d":"2017-04-04","q":"What's missing is the theatrical magic that might compensate for a score that feels more workmanlike than wonderful."},{"cn":"Jesse Green","o":"Vulture","s":30,"b":"Pan","t":1,"u":"https://www.vulture.com/2017/04/theater-review-amelie-a-new-musical.html","d":"2017-04-04","q":"The musical version of Amélie is so determined to be enchanting that it becomes exhausting instead."},{"cn":"Terry Teachout","o":"The Wall Street Journal","s":25,"b":"Pan","t":1,"u":"https://www.wsj.com/articles/amelie-a-new-musical-review-whimsy-without-magic-1491602403","d":"2017-04-07","q":"The problem with 'Amélie' is that it feels more like a theme-park ride than a musical—and not a very good ride at that."},{"cn":"David Gordon","o":"New York Theatre Guide","s":58,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://newyorktheatreguide.com/reviews/amelie-a-new-musical","d":"2017-04-12","q":"The musical adaptation captures some of the whimsy and charm of the original."},{"cn":"Casey Curtis","o":"Front Row Center","s":53,"b":"Negative","t":2,"u":"https://thefrontrowcenter.com/2017/04/a-homily-for-amelie/","d":"2017-04-08","q":"But overall this show is a lesson in messing with the sacred."}],"au":{"score":63,"designation":"Disliking","sources":{"mz":{"s":63,"c":184,"sr":3.1}}},"cn":{"t":"Critics find this musical adaptation charming but ultimately underwhelming, struggling to translate the film's whimsy to stage. The sweetness occasionally resonates, but more often feels precious and exhausting.","rc":7},"bo":{"tw":null,"at":{"g":5307176,"p":83,"a":64833}},"ta":"219 W 48th St, New York, NY 10036","vs":{"sl":4,"so":4,"co":2,"am":4,"fa":3},"pd":"2017-03-09","ca":[{"n":"Adam Chanler-Berat","r":"Nino"},{"n":"Phillipa Soo","r":"Amélie"},{"n":"Tony Sheldon","r":"Dufayel"},{"n":"David Andino","r":"Blind Beggar"},{"n":"Randy Blair","r":"Hipolito"},{"n":"Heath Calvert","r":"Lucien"},{"n":"Alison Cimmet","r":"Amandine"},{"n":"Savvy Crawford","r":"Young Amélie"},{"n":"Manoel Felciano","r":"Raphael"},{"n":"Harriett D. Foy","r":"Suzanne"},{"n":"Alyse Alan Louis","r":"Georgette"},{"n":"Maria-Christina Oliveras","r":"Gina"},{"n":"Paul Whitty","r":"Joseph"}]}